Package: rsvd
Type: Package
Title: Randomized Singular Value Decomposition
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2026-10-16
Authors@R: c(person("N. Benjamin", "Erichson", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "erichson@icsi.berkeley.edu"))
Author: N. Benjamin Erichson [aut, cre]
Maintainer: N. Benjamin Erichson <erichson@icsi.berkeley.edu>
Description: Computes low-rank matrix approximations for dimension reduction, data
  analysis, and data compression. Randomized algorithms form a small subspace
  from random combinations of the input and carry out the main factorization
  in that subspace. This can reduce computational work when the requested rank
  is small relative to the matrix dimensions and the input admits an accurate
  low-rank approximation. Methods include singular value decomposition,
  principal component analysis, QB factorization, interpolative and CUR
  decompositions, and robust principal component analysis. Selected methods
  support sparse matrices, including principal component analysis with
  implicit centering and scaling. Plotting functions display scores, loadings,
  and explained variance. The methods and their applications are described
  by Erichson et al. (2019) <doi:10.18637/jss.v089.i11>.
